    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nI wanted to try out having `search_method` set to `nearest`, and using a special prefix to instead use `search_method = \"cover\"` (similar to the existing next / last bindings). I tried replicating the functionality of these bindings myself, but the mapping logic calls private functions, and the only exposed function is `select_textobject()`, which takes a specific ID and isn't generalizable to all bindings.\n\nThis would be easily resolved if mini.ai exposed these bindings:\n```lua\n  mappings = {\n    around_cover = '',\n    inside_cover = ''\n  }\n```\nThey could be unmapped by default, changing nothing for users who don't want to use them.\n\nI have a patch for this locally that works great, but per the contributing docs, I wanted to put up an issue first.",
