        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI'm afraid, this is a bit too much to add configuration for. Especially since using `'next'` as the main search method is not recommended because it is not quite easily predictable (and, frankly, was added only for completeness sake). The main suggestion is to use `'cover'` as the main search method (although `'cover_or_next'` is the default) and use explicit mappings for `'next'` and `'last'` search methods.\n\n> ... the mapping logic calls private functions, and the only exposed function is `select_textobject()`, which takes a specific ID and isn't generalizable to all bindings.\n\nUsing `select_textobject` is still enough for implementing custom mappings which force specific search method. The complexity depends on how many edge cases you'd want to cover, but the straightforward `select_textobject('a', vim.fn.getcharstr(), { search_method = 'cover' })` already covers most cases.",
